# Matchup DNA website: hosting keys. Copy the part you need; never commit the real values (.env* is ignored by git).
#
# 1) On your laptop, in web/.env.upload: the uploader's read-and-write key (R2 API token "Object Read & Write",
#    limited to this one bucket). Used by web/scripts/upload-snapshot.mjs after each scheduled publish.
R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
R2_BUCKET=matchup-dna-site
R2_UPLOAD_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
R2_UPLOAD_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=

# 2) In Vercel (Project > Settings > Environment Variables): the site's read-only key (R2 API token "Object Read
#    only", limited to the same bucket). Never put the upload key in Vercel.
# R2_ACCOUNT_ID=
# R2_BUCKET=matchup-dna-site
# R2_READ_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# R2_READ_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
#
# Without R2 keys the site reads the local folders web/.data/snapshot and web/.data/history (development).
